WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.188
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online C one, Book four.

2
00:00:05.488 --> 00:00:09.141
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.441 --> 00:00:16.018
Unit eighteen: Corporate Ethics. Today you will express priorities with prioritizing X over Y.

4
00:00:16.318 --> 00:00:19.016
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.967 --> 00:00:23.408
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.250 --> 00:00:26.528
Corporate social responsibility.

7
00:00:27.517 --> 00:00:32.964
Corporate social responsibility means a company's commitment to benefit society and the environment.

8
00:00:33.550 --> 00:00:37.349
Their corporate social responsibility programme funds rural schools.

9
00:00:37.950 --> 00:00:41.450
Your turn. Say: Corporate social responsibility.

10
00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:46.706
Corporate social responsibility.

11
00:00:47.450 --> 00:00:48.718
Business ethics.

12
00:00:49.717 --> 00:00:53.609
Business ethics means moral principles applied to business decisions.

13
00:00:54.217 --> 00:00:58.109
Business ethics courses are now compulsory for MBA students.

14
00:00:58.717 --> 00:01:02.089
Your turn. Say: Business ethics.

15
00:01:04.933 --> 00:01:06.434
Business ethics.

16
00:01:07.183 --> 00:01:08.672
Stakeholder interest.

17
00:01:09.683 --> 00:01:14.574
Stakeholder interest means the concerns of anyone affected by a company's actions.

18
00:01:15.183 --> 00:01:18.448
The plan balanced shareholder and stakeholder interests.

19
00:01:19.050 --> 00:01:22.062
Your turn. Say: Stakeholder interest.

20
00:01:24.900 --> 00:01:26.377
Stakeholder interest.

21
00:01:27.117 --> 00:01:28.489
Sustainability.

22
00:01:29.483 --> 00:01:34.281
Sustainability means operating without damaging the future environment or society.

23
00:01:34.883 --> 00:01:38.497
Sustainability targets were added to managers' bonuses.

24
00:01:39.083 --> 00:01:42.096
Your turn. Say: Sustainability.

25
00:01:44.933 --> 00:01:46.201
Sustainability.

26
00:01:46.950 --> 00:01:48.288
Transparency.

27
00:01:49.283 --> 00:01:53.419
Transparency means openness and honesty about actions and information.

28
00:01:54.017 --> 00:01:57.084
Transparency about wages improved workers' trust.

29
00:01:57.683 --> 00:02:00.556
Your turn. Say: Transparency.

30
00:02:03.400 --> 00:02:04.645
Transparency.

31
00:02:05.383 --> 00:02:06.396
Whistleblower.

32
00:02:07.383 --> 00:02:11.937
Whistleblower means a person who exposes wrongdoing inside an organisation.

33
00:02:12.550 --> 00:02:15.420
A whistleblower revealed the safety violations.

34
00:02:16.017 --> 00:02:18.495
Your turn. Say: Whistleblower.

35
00:02:21.333 --> 00:02:22.358
Whistleblower.

36
00:02:23.117 --> 00:02:24.118
Compliance.

37
00:02:25.117 --> 00:02:28.300
Compliance means acting in accordance with laws and rules.

38
00:02:28.917 --> 00:02:31.822
Compliance is the minimum; ethics goes further.

39
00:02:32.417 --> 00:02:34.744
Your turn. Say: Compliance.

40
00:02:37.600 --> 00:02:38.729
Compliance.

41
00:02:39.483 --> 00:02:40.659
Integrity.

42
00:02:41.650 --> 00:02:46.239
Integrity means the quality of being honest and having strong moral principles.

43
00:02:46.850 --> 00:02:49.778
Her integrity earned the respect of the whole industry.

44
00:02:50.383 --> 00:02:53.012
Your turn. Say: Integrity.

45
00:02:55.867 --> 00:02:56.995
Integrity.

46
00:02:57.800 --> 00:03:01.416
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:03:02.250 --> 00:03:10.071
Visal, a factory could save money by delaying repairs to its fire exits. It's legal for another six months. Should it wait?

48
00:03:11.183 --> 00:03:20.340
Legally, perhaps. Ethically, no. A responsible company prioritizes workers' safety over short-term savings.

49
00:03:21.450 --> 00:03:23.426
But shareholders expect profit.

50
00:03:24.517 --> 00:03:35.200
They do, yet history shows that firms prioritizing profit over safety often pay far more later, through accidents, lawsuits and lost customers.

51
00:03:36.317 --> 00:03:39.199
And if an employee reports the problem publicly?

52
00:03:40.283 --> 00:03:48.764
Then the company should protect that whistleblower. Prioritizing reputation over honesty is exactly how scandals grow.

53
00:03:49.900 --> 00:03:51.342
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:52.183 --> 00:03:55.530
Grammar focus: Prioritizing X over Y.

55
00:03:55.830 --> 00:03:57.144
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:57.850 --> 00:04:01.812
Some companies prioritize stakeholders over short-term profit.

57
00:04:02.717 --> 00:04:05.691
A responsible firm puts safety before savings.

58
00:04:06.583 --> 00:04:10.115
Leaders who place integrity above convenience earn trust.

59
00:04:11.067 --> 00:04:22.847
Use 'prioritize X over Y' (not 'than Y'). Alternatives: put X before Y, place X above Y, give priority to X. The noun is 'priority': Safety is our top priority.

60
00:04:23.583 --> 00:04:27.640
Be careful! Don't say: They prioritize profit than people.

61
00:04:29.600 --> 00:04:32.679
Say: They prioritize profit over people.

62
00:04:32.979 --> 00:04:34.909
Prioritize X over Y.

63
00:04:35.700 --> 00:04:38.596
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:39.400 --> 00:04:40.865
Beyond Compliance.

65
00:04:41.165 --> 00:04:46.242
Corporate ethics asks not merely what a company may legally do, but what it ought to do.

66
00:04:47.233 --> 00:04:52.704
The shareholder view argues that firms should prioritize profit over other goals, provided they obey the law.

67
00:04:53.700 --> 00:05:00.703
The stakeholder view, by contrast, holds that companies must also consider workers, communities and the environment.

68
00:05:01.700 --> 00:05:10.294
Disasters such as the 2013 Rana Plaza collapse in Bangladesh showed the human cost of prioritizing low prices over safety.

69
00:05:11.300 --> 00:05:17.572
Today, investors increasingly reward firms whose integrity and transparency reduce long-term risks.

70
00:05:18.667 --> 00:05:22.843
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:05:23.683 --> 00:05:26.101
We should prioritize safety blank speed.

72
00:05:26.401 --> 00:05:29.160
A, than. B, over. C, from.

73
00:05:32.700 --> 00:05:34.734
The answer is B: over.

74
00:05:35.883 --> 00:05:40.008
A person who exposes wrongdoing inside an organisation is a blank.

75
00:05:40.308 --> 00:05:45.075
A, whistleblower. B, stakeholder. C, compliance officer.

76
00:05:48.633 --> 00:05:50.737
The answer is A: whistleblower.

77
00:05:51.883 --> 00:05:55.090
Honesty and strong moral principles describe blank.

78
00:05:55.390 --> 00:06:00.263
A, sustainability. B, transparency. C, integrity.

79
00:06:03.800 --> 00:06:06.159
The answer is C: integrity.

80
00:06:07.317 --> 00:06:09.154
Choose the correct sentence.

81
00:06:09.454 --> 00:06:16.230
A, They put profit before people.. B, They put profit than people.. C, They prioritize profit before than people..

82
00:06:19.767 --> 00:06:22.950
The answer is A: They put profit before people..

83
00:06:24.117 --> 00:06:28.369
According to the reading, the Rana Plaza collapse showed the cost of prioritizing…

84
00:06:28.669 --> 00:06:34.412
A, low prices over safety. B, workers over profit. C, law over ethics.

85
00:06:37.967 --> 00:06:40.930
The answer is A: low prices over safety.

86
00:06:42.133 --> 00:06:45.459
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:06:46.317 --> 00:06:51.082
Should a company prioritize shareholders or broader stakeholders? Why?

88
00:07:07.883 --> 00:07:09.360
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:07:09.660 --> 00:07:49.249
I believe a company should prioritize broader stakeholders, although shareholders deserve a fair return. A business depends on its workers, customers, suppliers and community; if it harms them, its long-term profits will eventually suffer too. For example, a factory that ignores safety may save money this year, but one accident could destroy its reputation and its contracts with international brands. Prioritizing stakeholders over short-term profit is therefore both ethical and, in the long run, commercially wise.

90
00:07:49.549 --> 00:07:51.398
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:07:52.283 --> 00:07:56.782
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and prioritizing x over y.

92
00:07:57.082 --> 00:08:01.719
Today's value is integrity. Do the right thing, even when no one is watching.

93
00:08:02.019 --> 00:08:04.614
See you in Unit nineteen. Goodbye!

94
00:08:04.914 --> 00:08:08.112
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

